Author-Name: Muñoz, Rafael
Author-Workplace-Name: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Recherches Economiques et Sociales (IRES)
Title: Skilled and Unskilled Employment in a Spanish Business Cycle Model
Abstract: We analyze to what extent skill heterogeneity in the labor market with different wage formation mechanisms can explain the features of the Spanish labor market. The model assumes two types of workers with differences in skills. Skilled labor sets wages in an efficiency way while unskilled labor does it through a union. We calibrate the model with Spanish data and assess it to account for differences in the labor market among skilled and unskilled workers.
Classification-JEL: E24; E32; J41; J51 
Keywords: Efficiency wage; unions; skilled-unskilled labor; business cycles
Length: 21
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, IRES
