Author-Name: de la Croix, David
Author-Workplace-Name: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Recherches Economiques et Sociales (IRES) ; Belgian National Fund for Scientific Research (FNRS)
Title: Standard-of-Living Aspirations and Economic Cycles
Abstract: Past experiences and social forces have been incorporated into tastes in order to analyze various microeconomic issues. We use these extended preferences to model the making of standard-of-living aspirations and study their effect on macroeconomic variables. We concentrate first on consumption behavior when there is habit formation. Such behavior is in accordance with several empirical facts and has important policy implications. Secondly, long term issues are analyzed assuming that children become habituated to a standard-of-living whilst still with their parents. This introduces a powerful mechanism responsible for long-term oscillations. We investigate in the third part whether habits applied to wage formation explain key labor market stylized facts.
Classification-JEL: E24; E32; O41
Keywords: Tastes; habit formation; cycles; fair wage; catching-up
Length: 24
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, IRES
Number: 2000008
Creation-Date: 2000-02-01
File-URL: http://sites.uclouvain.be/econ/DP/IRES/2000-8.pdf
File-Format: application/pdf
