Author-Name: Medeiros, João
Author-Workplace-Name: European Commission, Directorate General of Economic and Financial Affairs
Title: Endogenous Versus Exogenous Growth Facing a Fertility Shock
Abstract: This paper simulates the impact of a permanent fertility shock on economic growth, using endogenous versus exogenous growth OLG models. An endogenous growth model, with education as the engine of growth, dampens the negative impact of a decline in fertility on growth when compared with an exogenous growth model. This result stems from the rise in education levels brought about by the expectation of an increase in the discounted value of labour earnings.
Classification-JEL: D58; D91; E27; J13; J22; J24; O47
Keywords: Human capital; education; fertility; endogenous growth; simulation
Length: 33
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, IRES
Number: 2000017
Creation-Date: 2000-08-01
File-URL: http://sites.uclouvain.be/econ/DP/IRES/2000-17.pdf
