Author-Name: Bucci, Alberto
Author-Workplace-Name: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Recherches Economiques et Sociales (IRES)
Author-Name: Saglam, H.C.
Author-Workplace-Name: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Recherches Economiques et Sociales (IRES)
Title: Growth Maximizing Patent Life-Time
Abstract: Using a vertical differentiation model of endogenous growth with stochastic R&D activity, we characterize the optimal patent life-time the government would set in order to maximize economic growth. We show that a finite patent life-time does exist and is unique provided that the expected rate of return from R&D is sufficiently large. Additionally, we analyze the impact of the level of competition in R&D sector, the interest rate, the level of monopoly profit and the productivity parameter of research technology on this optimal patent life-time.
Classification-JEL: O31; O38; O41
Keywords: endogenous growth; patents life-time; innovation
