Author-Name: Vincent J. VANNETELBOSCH
Author-Workplace-Name: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Recherches Economiques et Sociales (IRES)
Title: Union Delegation and Incentives for Merger
Abstract: We analyze a unionized duopoly model to examine how unions affect the incentives for merger. We find that, once the union has the option to delegate, an increase in the union bargaining power can create incentives for the firms to merge.
Classification-JEL: J41;J50;J52
Keywords: Union delegation;Wage bargaining;Mergers
