Author-Name: Ana, MAULEON
Author-Name: Vincent, VANNETELBOSCH
Author-Workplace-Name: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Recherches Economiques et Sociales (IRES)
Title: Farsightedness and Cautiousness in Coalition Formation
Abstract: We adopt the largest consistent set defined by Chwe (J. of Econ. Theory 63 (1994, 299-235) to predict which coalition structures are possibly stable when prayers are farsighted.  We also introduce a refinement.  the largest cautious consistent set, based on the assumption that players are cautious.  For games with positive spillovers, many coalition structures may belong to the largest consistent set.  The grand coalition, which is the efficient coalition structure, always belongs to the largest consistent set and is the unique one to belong to the largest cautious consistent set.
Classification-JEL: C70; C71; C72; C78
Keywords: coalition formation, farsightedness, cautiousness, positive spillovers, largest consistent set
Length: 25
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, IRES
