Author-Name: Gilles, Joseph
Author-Workplace-Name: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Recherches Economiques et Sociales (IRES)
Author-Name: Olivier Pierrard
Author-Workplace-Name: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Recherches Economiques et Sociales (IRES)
Author-Name: Henri R. Sneessens 
Author-Workplace-Name: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Recherches Economiques et Sociales (IRES) - Belgique  and Université Catholique de Lille - France and IZA, Bonn - Duitschland
Title: Job Turnover, Unemployment and Labor Market Institutions
Abstract: This paper studies the role of labor market institutions on unemployment and on the cyclical properties of job flows.  We construct an intertemporal general equilibrium model with search unemployment and endogenous job turnover, and examine the consequences of introducing an unemployment benefit, a firing cost and a downward wage rigidity.  The simulations suggest that downward wage rigidities, rather than unemployment benefit or firing cost, may well play a dominant role in explaining both the high unemployment rate and the job flows dynamics of such an economy.
Classification-JEL: E24;J38;J63;J65
Keywords: Unemployment, Job flows dynamics, Institutions
Length: 27
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, IRES
