Author-Name: Abdeslam MARFOUK
Author-Workplace-Name: UNIVERSITE LIBRE DE BRUXELLES
Author-Name: Sara SALOMONE
Author-Workplace-Name: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Recherches Economiques et Sociales (IRES) and TOR VERGATA UNIVERSITY
Author-Name: Khalid SEKKAT
Author-Workplace-Name: UNIVERSITE LIBRE DE BRUXELLES
Title: Are skilled women more migratory than skilled men?
Abstract: This paper empirically studies emigration patterns of skilled males and females. In the most relevant model accounting for interdependencies between women and men’s decisions, we derive the gendered responses to traditional push factors. Females and males do not respond with the same intensity to the traditional determinants of labor mobility and gender-specific characteristics of the population at origin. Moreover, being other factors equal, the female willingness to follow the spouse seems to be much more pronounced with respect to the male one. From a quantitative perspective, our model reveals that skilled women are not more migratory than skilled men internationally, thus rejecting the existence of a genetic or social gender gap in international skilled migration.
Length: 30
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, IRES
